# Workshop gallery of Ancient Buildings Renew: one story, in one place, staged (PUBLISHING.md: every gallery capture is a staged photo).
#
# THE STORY (one, seven episodes, one summer day of the save, 5th of Septober, clear sky). Who: Nelim (Virginie), who keeps the last stop of an old road, and Shogun, her labrador, who is in every picture and always doing something (watches, sniffs, follows, waits at the machine, keeps the light); Soren, the steward of the Sanctuary, who buys his lunch at the machine like any traveller and shares the evening meal. Where: the calm zone (validated by the owner, VALIDE.md 2026-11-07), one square, seen from seven corners. Rhythm: hours 05, 09, 11, 12, 15, 21, 23; each episode starts where the one before ended. The thread is the WOOD: the first log at dawn to the cold brazier (1), stacked beside the fence she mends (2), fuel beside the stove (3), left beside the machine (4), left in the shade of the cold machine (5), burning in the torches and the brazier at dusk (6), tomorrow's first log carried out at night (7). Episodes: 1 she brings the first log of the day to the unlit brazier, between the old barrier and the fence; 2 she mends the fence in the morning; 3 she cooks at the stove at eleven; 4 at noon Soren buys his meal and Nelim takes the coin; 5 in the afternoon heat the old air conditioner keeps the food cold and the shade cool; 6 at dusk the six buildings stand lit together and they share the last meal; 7 at night the lamppost holds the dark and Nelim walks out of its light with tomorrow's first log. Miel and a lying Shogun are NOT used (not validated): Soren plays the second pawn, Shogun stands.
# Place for all seven: the calm zone of Nelim's tribe, a cream stone square (about 11 x 11 cells, x 195-205, z 181-191) with no roof and no wall shadow, ringed by flowers and bushes on soil (PickleTools/docs/SANCTUAIRE-LIEUX.md). Weather Clear. Each scene sets its own hour.
# Zoom N frames 2N cells high and 3.56N wide (SanctuaryBacklot/docs/GALERIE.md; a cell is 540 / N px on screen, 75 / N px on the 268 px Steam thumbnail). Decor placed by a scene is removed after its shot (`the decor is removed`); built things go with the save reload at the next scenario.
# GAME PAUSED MID-PLAY (owner, 2026-10-23): nobody stands facing the photographer. Each living thing faces what it does. A moving pawn is obtained by `I order "X" to (x, z)`, `game speed is normal`, `I let N ticks pass`, `game speed is paused`; the held item is put in the hands after the pause (`carries the item` holds on a paused game). `stands at ... facing D` only places a pawn that is meant to be still. Nobody is drafted (drafted pawns get the angry combat face). Faces: kit and brows per scene, held neutral, `normal+blink` last. Only Shogun faces the camera, in shot 7 (criterion c).
